    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0412" n="294" xml:id="pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/1072: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-13T14:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                                1928—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 13—6:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. My despatches Nos. 735 of January 18 and 746 of January 27th.<anchor n="60"
                        xml:id="d249-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign Affairs has informed me that he
                    has instructed the Japanese Minister of [<hi rendition="#italic">at</hi>] Peking
                    to confer with representatives of other foreign powers with a view to securing
                    adhesion of nonsignatory powers to the agreement of 1919 to [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">for</hi>?] the embargo of arms and ammunition for China.
                    The Minister for Foreign Affairs requested me to communicate this fact to my
                    Government and request my Government to instruct our Minister at Peking to give
                    active support to the Japanese Legation in this proposal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
